{"step_index":1007,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T19:11:13Z","content":"The design system has been refined to deliver an **executive-grade, modern, and visually comfortable** industrial AI interface.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Enhanced for Visual Comfort & Classy Aesthetics:\n\n1. **Refined Typography & Reading Flow**:\n   - Switched to **Plus Jakarta Sans** for headers, labels, and copy — providing crisp readability and professional presentation.\n   - Retained **JetBrains Mono** strictly for numerical telemetry, probabilities, percentages, and coordinates.\n\n2. **Executive Slate & Soothing Color Palette**:\n   - Replaced harsh saturated neons with a **deep obsidian slate canvas** (`#0b0f19`) accented by soft ambient radial gradients (ice blue, indigo, and emerald at 4–5% opacity).\n   - Card backgrounds now use a **velvet frosted glass treatment** (`rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65)`) with a subtle `rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12)` border and soft backdrop blur.\n   - Status badges use gentle, eye-friendly tones:\n     - **PASS / OPTIMAL**: Soft mint emerald (`#34d399` with `rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12)` background)\n     - **DEFECT / CRITICAL**: Elegant rose coral (`#fb7185` with `rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.12)` background)\n     - **UNCERTAIN / WARNING**: Warm champagne amber (`#fbbf24` with `rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12)` background)\n     - **NOVEL**: Soft lavender (`#c084fc` with `rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.12)` background)\n\n3. **Polished Interactive Visuals & Charts**:\n   - **Plotly Chart Engine**: Updated with gentle gridlines (`rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.08)`), matching typography, and refined data colors.\n   - **Plant Process Topology**: SCADA assembly nodes with smooth borders, subtle flow arrows (`&rarr;`), and clean station health metrics.\n   - **Confidence Bars**: Smooth, rounded progress bars with custom gradients.\n   - **What-If Simulation Cockpit**: Balanced sliders and dual metric cards.\n   - **Neural Architecture Card**: Clean HTML block detailing the input layer, 10 hidden tansig neurons, purelin output, and sub-millisecond forward-pass latency.\n\n4. **Zero Glare & Strict Rule Compliance**:\n   - **Zero emojis** anywhere in the code or interface.\n   - **Zero mentions of \"NEURAX 3.0\"** — standardized to *\"Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform\"*."}
